intro='''CODEX — TWELVE EVOCATION CANTRIPS: COMPLETE SOURCE CONFERENCE, NOT EXACT-CARD REVIEW.

Your rank-three Enchantment approval is preserved and implemented: eight cards and the integration manuscript are promoted, 23 preservation checks and 42 pipeline checks / 89,040 access boundaries pass. Catalog now237 reviewed/611 unfinished, 176 unfinished with actual class rank0–3. Only the recorded three editorial review-status phrases changed in cards; your Mental Chains cross-plane interpretation is explicit in the shared manuscript. Prior229 operational records, all original sources and all class cards are unchanged. Human balance/runtime/whole-game flow remain open. The owner requires cosmology review ONLY AFTER successful GitHub push and remote verification; keep that sequence, and do not review cosmology here.

We now need to reconcile these twelve UNFINISHED cantrips. All fourteen source placements/Core blocks, historical-alias fields and exact actual class-access rows follow. V,S only throughout: do not add F or import another game's familiar versions. All actual ranks are0, base0RP. New attack/save formulas, duration, geometry, targeting restrictions and other missing procedures must be clearly identified as NEW playtest completions, rather than presented as original canon. Retain all source variants even when unified mechanically. No automatic level scaling unless specifically proposed and justified. This conference does not approve final authored cards.

Established constraints: known/prepared access and actual class rank govern each cast. V audible, S usable free hand. Perceived target or point with line of effect; total cover normally blocks. Spell attack=1d20+PB+actual casting modifier versus AC (natural1 miss,20 hit/critical damage dice only). Spell save DC=8+PB+actual casting modifier, binary saves with no automatic natural1/20. Refrain applies on repeated same-ID actual casts, including cantrips; base D0 does not waive Refrain. A paid cast commits costs, concentration transition and cast-begin hooks before the counter window, then outcome hooks; countered casts do not refund. Ready casts commit at preparation, not later release. Ordinary Echo/copy effects do not proc/reproduce resources, but Arcane Echo expressly says cast again and needs an explicit actual-cast versus copy decision. No spell grants an extra action budget merely by changing a casting type.

One-round hostile riders use one FUTURE target regular END, excluding the entire current target turn; 6elapsed seconds outside initiative. One-minute caster effects use ten future caster regular STARTs (exclude the current), 60seconds outside, with existing clock transition rules. Original source wording such as 'next turn' may require a distinct onset. Same numerical slow family competes from pre-control Speed, strongest only, then separate system modifiers; spent movement never resets. Reaction denial is prospective (cannot erase an already committed stack item), and is not whole-Action hard control. Damage immunity is distinct from rider immunity unless the new rule explicitly requires positive damage. Positive post-defense/pre-temp-HP damage packets differ from actual loss including absorbed temporary HP. Do not inadvertently make riders depend on actual HP loss.

Fire damage or igniting an ordinary object does not automatically impose Burning; only an effect expressly inflicting that condition does. Environmental fire follows existing mundane fire procedures. Cold damage is not automatic Frozen/Rooted. Under HEALING_DEATH_PLAYTEST.md broad HP-gain prohibitions reduce legal healing and genuine excess to0; ordinary healing costs still commit, actual-HP reserve expenditure does not occur at0gain. Independent temporary HP, stabilization and other non-HP components remain. Returned HP of a resurrection LIFE TRANSITION is not ordinary healing and is not blocked by generic living HP-gain prohibitions; explicit corpse/soul blockers are a separate source. Please keep Chill Touch within that boundary, without conducting cosmology review.

Questions requiring finite, playable source dispositions:

1 Freezing Touch: preserve1d4cold, Touch. Supply melee spell attack if agreed. Source says '-5ft movement NEXT TURN', not simply an immediate round: decide exact onset (next regular target START?) and endpoint, current-turn exclusion, outside-combat procedure and overlapping/recast slow behavior. Decide hit versus positive-damage trigger; no automatic Frozen. Do not silently convert next-turn wording into immediate slowing.

2 Flame Lash: explicit 'melee range' conflicts with30ft metadata. Choose and justify an operational range/attack package, retaining both sources. Does a30ft melee spell attack preserve both, or should source effect take precedence at physical reach? Define one creature/object, ignition on qualifying hit, ordinary fuel and worn/carried targeting. No automatic Burning or ignition bypass of object defenses.

3 Soundburst: range5ft plus '5-ft AoE' needs center/shape; suggest a perceived point within5ft and5ft-radius sphere, but label this NEW. Specify all creatures including caster/allies if geometrically included, center line of effect and initial saves. CON fail1d4thunder+Deafenedone round, successnone. Decide independent Deafened immunity versus thunder-damage immunity and no ongoing aura.

4 Minor Combustion:30ftAction, ignite torch/small object. Bound physical size, adequate ignitable fuel, damp/nonflammable material, held/worn object consent and environmental effect. Avoid either unbounded structural arson or erasing the source ignition utility. No resource conjuring, creature attack or automatic Burning. A small ignited object can cause ordinary subsequent mundane hazards.

5 Force Needle: preserve1d6PIERCING despite name. Suggest ranged spell attack, ignore partial-cover AC bonus, retain total-cover/line-of-effect and perception requirements. Source says 'ignores cover' without qualification, so record total-cover boundary as NEW limitation. Define creature/object scope and no unintended force damage, armor bypass or through-wall oracle.

6 Arcane Echo: BonusAction,30ft, 'Next damaging cantrip can be cast again as bonus action', Instantaneous metadata inadequate. Need complete finite procedure: recipient self or willing creature at30ft; arming window; identify next qualifying cantrip at paid commitment, miss/countered originals, Ready preparation/release, when permission becomes usable, how long second-cast window lasts when arming spent this turn's BonusAction. Does this create a genuine new spell cast (own costs/components/targets/rolls/Counterspell/cadence/Refrain) with only casting-action substitution, or a copy? Source favors actual cast, but explicitly rule that. Qualification by chosen cantrip's printed damaging mode, not whether it actually injured; healing/non-damaging utility doesn't qualify. Reaction cantrips require original trigger for echo repeat or exclude such original activation modes? Avoid stolen spell knowledge, spell-copy recursion, Echo-generated repeat consuming another arm, multiple Echo charges/stacking and unlimited long-term stockpiling. Decide whether activation is prospectively limited to Action damaging cantrips (NEW limitation) to keep original reaction triggers intact. Preserve Universal Cantrip Echo as a separate future identity. We need one coherent source-fidelity choice, not several alternatives left to each table.

7 Shocking Grasp: preserve REACTION and30ft metadata; source does NOT sayTouch (unlike Freezing/Chill). Need explicit perceivable legal trigger, exact pre/post-trigger resolution and attack/save, plus1d8lightning and reaction-denial endpoint. No foreign game's Action/touch rewrite. Suggest triggered by a creature within30ft committing an Action on its own turn, aftercommitbeforeoutcome, ranged spell attack; but weigh broad at-will reaction-damage opportunity and distinguish balance concern from manuscript fidelity. Denial never cancels pending Reaction/Action or retroactively prevents its cast, and no unprinted metal-armor advantage. Decide how current-turn exclusion affects restriction.

8 Dancing Lights: both Evocation and Illusion identical up-to-four torch-sized lights,30ft,Action. Need duration/concentration, real illumination behavior for both actual schools, explicit bright/dim radii, creation positions, movement instruction/maximum, tether and barriers, recast ownership cap. Focused reviewed-playtest search found no general torch-radius rule; any numerical radius must be NEW, not claimed canonical. Existing Flicker Flame is fixed10ftdim/noheat/no movement; Resonance Mote5ftdim follows recipient. New Dancing Lights may legitimately illuminate more: do not confuse actual Illusion school with mere illusory image automatically. No heat/fuel/sunlight/damage/physical objects, no free reveal Invisible/Hidden or darkness dispel. IfConc selected, mark new and use actual concentration transition.

9 Acid Splash:1d6acid to one OR two targets at30ft. Resolution missing: propose independent DEX saves for creatures, no damage success, one damage roll shared among failed targets. No proximity requirement is printed; do not import a5ft pair-separation limit without acknowledging new constraint. Define creature/object eligibility; preserve two-target useful effect. No residual acid or armor-corrosion rider without source.

10 Chill Touch: both Evocation/Necromancy Action/Touch/VS,1d8necrotic and HP-gain prevention. Melee spell attack and exact rider deadline missing. Decide hit vs positive damage; one future target END newly completes duration. Healing prohibition follows the existing HP-gain/life-transition boundary stated above, no special Undead rider, no unlimited anti-resurrection seal. Preserve actual access to both schools.

11 Thunderclap: Action5ft,1d6thunder to ALL creatureswithin5ft. Need whether caster included; printed all suggests include unless explicit NEW exemption justified. Suggest caster-centered5ft sphere, line of effect, CON save negates (NEW; not printed). Distinguish from Soundburst's1d4+Deafened. Do not merge with distinct rank1 'Thunder Clap' ID thunder-clap. Define noise only as normally perceptible/no fixed hundreds-of-feet alarm range invented.

12 Poison Spray: Action10ft,1d12poison, explicitCONnegates. One perceived creature with line of effect, no separate attack, no Poisoned condition or persistent cloud. No unprinted inhalation/breathing/body-type exclusions; actual poison immunity/resistance handles damage. Confirm unchanged damage and no level scaling.

Please return a source disposition for each of twelve and a shared integration checklist, clearly marking NEW completions and conflicts. Flag any remaining evidence needed rather than declaring exact approval. Be particularly explicit for Arcane Echo, Freezing Touch onset and Shocking Grasp trigger. Neither this conference nor per-card work closes the wider game or the owner's eventual joint final flow/push gate.

COMPLETE SOURCE DATA (all fields retained; compact JSON):
'''
